Electron is a 1/2 spin.

00:59:03.420 --> 00:59:06.360
And electron obey the
power exclusion principle.

00:59:06.360 --> 00:59:10.980
So each quantum state can
only have maximum electron.

00:59:10.980 --> 00:59:19.140
But each quantum state, here,
this k for specific k value

00:59:19.140 --> 00:59:22.770
represents the wave function,
a vibrational wave function,

00:59:22.770 --> 00:59:24.570
that's quantum state.

00:59:24.570 --> 00:59:27.810
Each quantum state can have n--

00:59:27.810 --> 00:59:31.110
could be 0, 1, to
infinite of phonons.

00:59:34.290 --> 00:59:36.240
So those are bosons.

00:59:36.240 --> 00:59:39.780
And it's fundamentally
different.

00:59:39.780 --> 00:59:41.670
And it doesn't have a rest mass.

00:59:41.670 --> 00:59:42.810
Electron has a mass.

00:59:45.770 --> 00:59:48.860
What's a mass of photon?

00:59:48.860 --> 00:59:51.920
There's no rest mass, photon.

00:59:51.920 --> 00:59:52.802
It has a momentum.

00:59:52.802 --> 00:59:53.510
It has an energy.

00:59:56.070 --> 00:59:59.130
So you look, either you
can create the pressure

00:59:59.130 --> 01:00:01.290
but doesn't have a mass.

01:00:01.290 --> 01:00:05.140
It's a collective vibration,
it's collective modes.

01:00:05.140 --> 01:00:08.290
So I joked.

01:00:08.290 --> 01:00:11.578
I had once a colleague say
after he sit in my class,

01:00:11.578 --> 01:00:13.120
I still don't know
what is a photon--

01:00:13.120 --> 01:00:14.920
a phonon.

01:00:14.920 --> 01:00:21.520
And it's a fictitious
particle sometimes people say.

01:00:21.520 --> 01:00:25.310
It's not a real particle.

01:00:25.310 --> 01:00:29.540
It's a-- so this is a phonon.

01:00:29.540 --> 01:00:36.290
It has an energy and
it has momentum hk.

01:00:36.290 --> 01:00:39.970
And in 3D, it's k.

01:00:39.970 --> 01:00:45.360
Or energy sometimes we
write as h bar omega.

01:00:45.360 --> 01:00:49.560
Your h nu, depends on
whether you use nu or omega.

01:00:52.390 --> 01:00:59.280
So that's the phonons.

01:00:59.280 --> 01:01:02.700
And now you go to, like I
said, you go to real crystal,

01:01:02.700 --> 01:01:06.030
you will see different phonon--

01:01:06.030 --> 01:01:08.520
different direction have
a different dispersion.

01:01:08.520 --> 01:01:12.660
So again, I will go
